<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Beginners Rainy Weather</h1>
<p>Rain is the part of Hanoi riding that most beginner guides politely skip, and it is exactly the part a new rider needs to hear about first. Hanoi's wet months arrive in heavy, short bursts, and a beginner on a rented 50cc will meet them sooner or later, usually sooner. The honest position is simple: a 50cc is a fine beginner machine in dry weather and a manageable one in wet weather, provided the rider prepares, slows down, and knows when to stop and wait. The rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, rents 50cc scooters and motorbikes at 200,000 VND per day, and rainy days are a good moment to ask the team about gear and wet-weather handling before you ride out.</p>
<p>This guide belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental</a> hub, pairs with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost breakdown</a>, and complements the answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The general city-wide advice lives in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-a-motorbike-in-hanoi-rainy-season/">rainy season riding guide</a>; this page keeps it specific to a beginner on a small bike.</p>
